WHY 06 IS THE RIGHT PROBE. 06 was purpose-built (ADR-0154) to test the real-work
slice every other task misses: inferring a codebase's conventions from the
codebase, not the prompt. The prompt asks only for "a renderer that outputs YAML".
CONTRIBUTING.md + two sibling renderers state FOUR hard, interpreter-unenforced
conventions:
  R1 stdlib-only (import yaml WORKS — pyyaml installed — but is FORBIDDEN);
  R2 raise PluginError, never a builtin;
  R3 @register("name") + class in __all__;
  R4 add a case to the existing parametrized test, don't write a new test fn.
A complete-but-wrong on 06 = working code that violates a convention — the exact
failure a "better on small models" lever (or verify_auto) must prove it catches.

